N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): every second of the clip was reduced to its strongest five pitches (harmonic salience, the steady room tone subtracted); from 5 s on, the chords change about every 0.98 s, and the sequence D (held) | G Bm A D | G Bm A D | D D | G Bm A D | G Bm A D | D D was read, with the low pipes on G3, B2, A2 and D3; matching major and minor triads beat by beat confirmed it (D, B minor and A strongest; the G chord scored as E minor in the first passes).
N:UNCERTAIN: the first chord of each phrase (G and B sound with E: G with an added sixth, or E minor; a pipe between G and G sharp is heard at 21.6 s); whether the chord on B is B minor or a D chord over B; the metre (written here in 2/4, two chords a bar); the B flat that sounds against the D chords; the top line (E6 and C6 are the strongest high pitches, not a tune).
